00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.863
and start ramming the
Icelandic coast guard boats.

00:12:20.863 --> 00:12:22.145
- [Narrator] Continued the skirmish

00:12:22.145 --> 00:12:23.603
which ended in yet another (mumbles).

00:12:23.603 --> 00:12:24.975
(horn blaring)

00:12:24.975 --> 00:12:28.250
(upbeat music)

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:32.510
- No more warning shots, no
more soft core standoffs,

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.800
we are now ramming each other.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.800
This leads to a series of
standoffs in the North Atlantic,

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.960
between Icelandic coast
guard and the Royal Navy,

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.183
the most powerful Navy on earth.

00:12:46.813 --> 00:12:47.646
(exclaiming loudly)

00:12:47.646 --> 00:12:48.500
These fish and chips people,

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.200
they love their fish and chips.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.294
- It's really good.

00:12:51.294 --> 00:12:52.127
(laughing loudly)

00:12:52.127 --> 00:12:52.960
It's delicious.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.327
- So, does Iceland back down
in the second Cod War and say,

00:12:55.327 --> 00:12:58.317
"Okay, fine, the International
Court ruled against us,

00:12:58.317 --> 00:13:02.557
"Britain and West Germany
and Denmark don't like this,

00:13:02.557 --> 00:13:03.700
"we're just gonna chill out."

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.560
No, they didn't, they
kept it up and in fact,

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.590
they decided to pull out their
one major piece of leverage

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:14.670
in all of this, which was
their alliance with NATO.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:18.070
- [Narrator] NATO land is
composed of 14 different nations

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.200
with a combined army, 7 million strong.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.910
- Easily, my favorite part about Iceland

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.420
is that you can be driving through

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:27.730
some random mountain paths,
like we've been doing,

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:32.730
at midnight and you can
wander upon waterfall

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.500
after waterfall, after
waterfall that are just there.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.333
They're just there.

00:13:36.333 --> 00:13:40.170
Just look at this waterfall
that I'm looking at.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.833
It is insane.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.560
Iceland was a member of NATO.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.910
- [Narrator] NATO was
founded April four, 1949

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:54.020
by 12 nations of widely
different languages and customs.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.480
During its six years,

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.930
NATO has well proved it's power for peace.

00:13:57.930 --> 00:14:00.770
- And they occupied a
fairly important role

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.450
because of where they exist,

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.370
they exist right here
in the North Atlantic,

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.650
a very strategic place.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:10.280
So Iceland decides to
pull out their wild card,

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.190
the thing that they've been
holding onto this whole time,

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:15.090
which is we will withdraw from NATO

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:19.030
if you do not recognize our
50 nautical mile boundary

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.340
of the ocean.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.480
If Iceland withdraws from NATO,

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:24.680
because of something the British did,

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.250
the US is gonna be pissed at Britain.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.827
- No, let go of him (yells).

00:14:28.827 --> 00:14:30.066
- Tell that bitch to be cool.

00:14:30.066 --> 00:14:31.988
- I'm gonna kill you.
- Say, bitch, be cool.

00:14:31.988 --> 00:14:33.561
- Be cool, honey bunny.
- Say, bitch, be cool.

00:14:33.561 --> 00:14:34.690
- Be cool.
- Tell that fucking bitch

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.011
to chill!

00:14:36.011 --> 00:14:37.140
- Be cool, honey bunny.
- Chill that

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.350
fucking bitch out!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.757
- So Britain was like,

00:14:39.757 --> 00:14:41.800
"Okay fine, you win 50 miles, you got it."

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.240
- Gosh, darn it, I give up.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.630
It's yours, you can have it.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.188
- Cod Wars, Episode Two is over.

00:14:47.188 --> 00:14:48.021
(ringing softly)

00:14:48.021 --> 00:14:49.117
Iceland wins again (laughs).

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:53.190
So this is now the
second time that Iceland,

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:58.190
this tiny country with no
military has like bested

00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:00.240
one of the most powerful
countries on earth,

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.310
all because of fish.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.660
They freaking love fish here,

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:05.160
like don't mess with Iceland's fish.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.450
But this isn't over.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.130
It's the 1970s

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:12.090
and we are about to commence
Cod War, Episode Three,

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.414
Return of the Cod.

00:15:13.414 --> 00:15:15.831
(soft music)

00:15:22.214 --> 00:15:25.047
(mumbling softly)

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:33.110
Officially made it to the
Western most point of Europe.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.020
I think that's right,

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.210
I mean, we tried to say

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.620
we were in the Western most point of view

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.450
like two years ago, in this moment.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.510
- [Narrator] Just a 30 minute drive

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.010
outside of downtown Sintra

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:43.020
is the Western most point
of continental Europe.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.570
- And yeah, that obviously wasn't, I mean,

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:46.930
it was like continental Europe.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.290
So now we, here we are again,

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.640
in the Western most point
of Europe right here.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.730
I don't know where we are, but
we're really freaking west.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.810
We've been driving for like
four hours on dirt roads

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:02.995
to get to this cliff on
this very tip of Iceland

00:16:02.995 --> 00:16:04.649
on the west fjords.

00:16:04.649 --> 00:16:07.300
You know, we're here to see puffins.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.700
What are we here to see son?

00:16:11.046 --> 00:16:12.909
- Puffins?
- Yes.

00:16:12.909 --> 00:16:15.326
(soft music)

00:16:17.878 --> 00:16:18.800
- Dad, wait for me.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.400
- I'm waiting for you, big team.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.370
Man, these puffins are just right here.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.540
They were just right under
our nose the whole time,

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.373
look at this.

00:16:34.507 --> 00:16:36.460
I mean, I guess I'd seen puffins

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:41.360
like on Instagram or
something, but I had no idea

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.840
just how striking these birds are.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:48.500
This is, photographing these birds today

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:53.387
has been just it's really
helped me appreciate them.

00:17:07.789 --> 00:17:10.539
(waves crashing)

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.160
Episode Three is basically a repeat

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.820
of the last two episodes.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.460
The British move into these
waters to get their little fish

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:21.140
because they want fish and chips.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.800
More ramming, tons more
ramming, more standoffs.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:27.100
Britain is not okay with this tiny country

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:27.933
pushing them around.

00:17:27.933 --> 00:17:29.130
I mean, it's Britain, they're
used to just literally

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:31.930
taking over any country
they want in the whole world

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:33.140
and they're being told what to do

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:36.040
by this little tiny island
nation, they're not liking it.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:36.900
What I love about Iceland

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.850
is that they don't just dig in
their heels and not concede,

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.160
they would push a little bit further.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.017
So this time they're like,

00:17:42.017 --> 00:17:43.687
"We don't just want 50 nautical miles,

00:17:43.687 --> 00:17:47.287
"we want 200 nautical miles off our coast

00:17:47.287 --> 00:17:49.690
"for exclusive fishing."

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:52.837
Britain is like, "No, this is not good,

00:17:52.837 --> 00:17:56.310
"how are we getting bested
every time we try to fish?"

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:59.170
This got so bad that the UK and Iceland

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.930
actually broke off diplomatic relations.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.740
They were like really angry at each other

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:05.367
until the Americans come
in and they're like,

00:18:05.367 --> 00:18:06.850
"Dude, stop it."

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.700
NATO, the cold war, nuclear weapons,

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.410
like stop crying over your fish and chips,

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:13.820
we have bigger priorities.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.380
- Chill out Dick word.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.410
- And so they backed down

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.860
and they recognize the
200 nautical mile claim

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:22.080
that Iceland was asserting.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.420
It turns out a couple of
years later, the UN developed

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:28.120
the United Nations
Convention On Law of the Sea,

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.150
a big document that actually codifies

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.810
that every country gets 200 nautical miles

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:36.400
of exclusive economic activity.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:39.190
But Iceland was already
thinking in these terms,

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:41.730
they're like the exclusive
economic zone hipsters,

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.490
like they were far (chuckles)
ahead of everyone else.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:46.907
(soft music)

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:54.010
There are always sheep on
the side of the road here,

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:58.050
including loads of baby
sheep that are so precious,

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.750
it always seems like
they're about to dart out

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:00.690
in front of the side of the road,

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:03.343
giving us loads of anxiety,
but they're very cute.

00:19:13.875 --> 00:19:15.510
She has never seen rain deer before,

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:19.773
so she's taking in the reindeer.

00:19:27.056 --> 00:19:29.310
(exclaiming softly)

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.240
Pretty special?

00:19:31.119 --> 00:19:33.007
- Unbelievable.

00:19:33.007 --> 00:19:34.890
- So, what are the Cod Wars teach us?

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:37.670
Well, as an international relations guy,

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.810
I'm sorta like, this doesn't square up

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.920
with a lot of the theories
that I learned in school.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:45.670
In school, we learned
that when countries trade

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:49.560
with each other and with when
they're bound by alliances,

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:52.520
they tend to cooperate better than ever.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.100
In this case, what you see

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.820
is countries that are bound to each other

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:59.040
through Alliance and through
trade who are not cooperating

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.160
because they are bound to each other

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:02.950
by trade and institutions.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:06.010
In fact, one of the major
bargaining chips in the war

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:10.250
was the fact that Iceland
was gonna withdraw from NATO.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:13.160
They use the institution as leverage.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.440
- [Narrator] We have declared
that the Icelandic law

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:21.440
will be upheld and I have on
that law, nothing more cliche.

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.530
- All I have to say, this
is a super unique case

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.460
of a tiny country using its leverage

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.570
to basically make

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.130
one of the most powerful
countries in the world concede

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.860
and it totally worked.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:37.260
- This is me, all right,
I'm not a fucking athlete,

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:40.080
this is my fucking way,
this is how I work.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.747
- But the bigger lesson
for me is, and the thing

00:20:41.747 --> 00:20:45.450
I'm gonna take away, is
don't (beeps) with Iceland

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:46.672
when it comes to fish.

00:20:46.672 --> 00:20:47.550
(ringing softly)

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:48.833
Okay, see you later.

